WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.339
Have a gun license?

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:03.920
Plan to bring your gun to my home town

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:05.460
next time you fly in?

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.160
“Pack all unloaded firearm and firearm parts in a locked

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:10.300
hard-sided container.”

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.620
If you call the TSA, they will tell you

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.280
to put the gun in a locked container and:

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.360
“notify the airline during the ticket counter

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:18.560
check-in process.”

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.780
But even if you do this properly,

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:23.820
New York authorities will still wreck your life.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.560
I declared my gun, because I always do.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.540
I travel, I fly in and out all over the US with it.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.439
Patricia Jordan carries her gun for protection.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.940
She correctly followed all the TSA procedures

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:35.880
when she flew from her home in Georgia to

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.080
New York City.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.300
It’s in the TSA case,

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.520
everything’s separate.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:41.729
It’s locked.

00:00:41.729 --> 00:00:44.040
She was traveling with three teenage girls,

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.340
and wanted her gun in her hotel room.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:47.980
I know that if something happens

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.540
that I can protect myself.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:50.860
I was glad that she brought it

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:52.840
just in case something did happen.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:53.860
On their way home,

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:56.280
Patricia did everything correctly again.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.820
The airline counter she again

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.740
told the agent she wanted to check her gun.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:02.440
But this time she was told,

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:03.080
“Wait.”

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:04.020
The next thing I know they’re

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:05.520
getting ready to arrest me.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.500
For what exactly?

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.400
For having a gun.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.500
I thought I was going to pass out,

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.140
I really did.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.060
I have my permit.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:13.770
I’m doing everything I’m supposed to right.

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:14.980
Of course I started freaking out.

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:16.580
She sat there and begged the lady,

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:17.520
"Please don’t arrest my mom,

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:18.500
please don’t arrest my mom."

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.580
She's like crying, begging her not to take me.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:24.120
The police put Patricia in jail and told her,

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:25.780
you’ve committed a felony.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:28.240
The minimum was 3 and a half to 7 years

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.100
mandatory prison for this.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.840
Another visitor, Avi Wolf

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:34.680
was jailed just for having a gun part,

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.180
an empty magazine.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:37.580
There were no bullets?

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:38.960
It was just something like this?

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:40.240
It was exactly like that.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.380
Instead of a plastic exterior mine had

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:43.820
a little bit of a different make to it

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:45.320
but it was exactly that.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:47.100
Somebody could’ve done more damage

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.880
to an individual with a fork from McDonald’s

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:50.980
than with that.

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:53.940
Wolf too checked with the TSA beforehand.

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:57.940
They told him, just declare it to TSA agents at security.

00:01:57.940 --> 00:01:59.140
I telling them that,

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:01.880
just a notification I have a magazine here.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.440
It’s empty, there’s no bullets,

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:05.760
there’s no gunpowder.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.920
You know, I called TSA before doing it,

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.940
and this is what they told me to do, to declare it.

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:10.620
The next thing I know

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.420
they’re pulling me over to the side

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:14.720
and they're all like

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:15.880
Do you know what you have in your bag?

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:17.700
And I'm like,&nbsp;I know what I have in my bag,

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.640
I told you what I have in my bag.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:21.220
Fast forward about an hour

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:24.360
and it was 4 Port Authority police officers were there,

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:26.600
the chief of LaGuardia airport is there.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:29.360
Like, I mean, they thought they found

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:31.620
somebody trying to do 9/11 repeat.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:32.700
For this?

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:33.480
Literally.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:34.160
For that.

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:35.620
They asked me if I had a gun license.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:37.420
Of course I had a gun license.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:38.460
I’m from Georgia,

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.500
everybody there’s got a gun license.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.460
And they’re like, well sir,

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:44.080
you’re going to be getting arrested now.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:45.560
I’m like, oh, no.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.720
The other prisoners couldn’t believe why Avi was in jail.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.360
One guy beat up his wife,

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:53.580
this other guy was busted for a whole bunch of drugs.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.260
So they’re like, what did you do?

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:56.560
Why are you here?

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:57.489
It's like

00:02:57.489 --> 00:03:00.400
I got caught at security with an empty magazine.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.299
What did they say?

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.640
Just laughed at me; like it was a joke.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:05.380
But it was no joke.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:09.060
Avi and Patricia were released after a day in jail.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:11.760
But they still faced that felony charge.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:13.120
I could barely function,

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.440
I had to get on like anxiety medicine.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:17.050
I was throwing up every day.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:19.180
Months later, New York allowed each to plead

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:20.700
guilty to a lesser charge:

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.500
public disorder.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:26.320
But it cost each $15,000 in legal fees.

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:28.400
Why does New York City do this to people?

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.579
They need to spend a day in jail?

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:32.860
We get them through the system as quick as we can.

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:34.520
District Attorney Jack Ryan

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.900
handles New York airport gun charges.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.320
We are not going to apologize

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:39.460
for enforcing our gun laws.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:41.420
We do enforce them fairly

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:44.340
and humanely and as compassionately as we can.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:47.000
Is it a fair system when it costs them,

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:51.200
15, 17 thousand dollars and they spend a day in jail?

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:53.980
It’s as fair as we can make it

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:55.860
under all of those circumstances.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:57.359
Even in Avi’s case?

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.900
It’s an empty piece of plastic.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:01.600
Whether the magazine is made out of plastic,

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:03.580
Kevlar, or metal I think is immaterial to make

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:04.880
a question of how many bullets it holds.

00:04:04.889 --> 00:04:06.340
That’s why New York has banned them.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:09.760
Isn’t what’s material is whether it held any bullets?

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:10.320
It didn’t.

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:11.040
It was empty.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:12.960
You can discuss that with the legislature.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.500
They didn’t make it a crime

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:15.680
only if there’s bullets in it.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:16.860
They made it a crime.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:19.580
Patricia had carefully separated her gun

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:20.460
from her bullets.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.880
The officer could not even find my bullets

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:24.040
in my suitcase;

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:25.500
I had to stop

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:27.700
and go show him where they were.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:28.800
But yet they said

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:31.720
that this was considered a loaded weapon in New York.

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:33.680
Under New York law if they’re together

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:34.680
they’re loaded.

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:37.180
And so we have prosecuted a number of those cases.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:38.800
They are loaded even if they’re not loaded?

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:41.260
If the weapon and the ammunition are together

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:42.220
they’re loaded.

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:44.840
Most every week, New York jails someone who

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:48.000
innocently travels with a gun, legally licensed

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.000
in their state.

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:50.540
These are people who are trying to do everything right.

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.200
They go onto the TSA website,

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:55.100
they follow the regulations to fly with their gun.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:56.560
They go

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:58.100
on the airline website

00:04:58.100 --> 00:04:59.360
and they follow the regulations

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:00.600
to properly fly with their gun.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.420
And then New York jails them.

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:05.800
You’re a sadistic bully locking these people up.

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.700
These aren’t threats

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:09.560
We know they’re not threats

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:10.710
after we check them out.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.200
We do not know who they are

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:13.460
when we first talk to them.

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:14.740
Give me a break.

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:16.680
Prosecutors have discretion;

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:18.680
they could be reasonable with these

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:19.760
poor people

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:21.380
who had no idea that they’d violated

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.680
New York’s strange laws.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:25.820
But New York politicians don’t want you

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:26.860
to have a gun.

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:29.080
So they will put you in jail

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:30.980
to send everyone a message.

